{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/virtualized-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtualized-columns"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtualized-rows (dynamic row height)"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtualized-rows (fixed row height)"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/virtualized-infinite-scrolling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"virtualized-infinite-scrolling"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"virtualization-guide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Virtualization Guide"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The TanStack Table packages do not come with any virtualization APIs or features built-in, but TanStack Table can easily work with other virtualization libraries like "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-window","children":[{"type":"text","value":"react-window"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or TanStack's own "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/virtual/v3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Virtual"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This guide will show some strategies for using TanStack Table with TanStack Virtual."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"virtualization-guide","text":"Virtualization Guide","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [virtualized-columns](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-columns)\n- [virtualized-rows (dynamic row height)](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows)\n- [virtualized-rows (fixed row height)](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows)\n- [virtualized-infinite-scrolling](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-infinite-scrolling)\n\n## Virtualization Guide\n\nThe TanStack Table packages do not come with any virtualization APIs or features built-in, but TanStack Table can easily work with other virtualization libraries like [react-window](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-window) or TanStack's own [TanStack Virtual](https://tanstack.com/virtual/v3). This guide will show some strategies for using TanStack Table with TanStack Virtual.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Virtualization Guide\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [virtualized-columns](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-columns)\n- [virtualized-rows (dynamic row height)](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows)\n- [virtualized-rows (fixed row height)](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-rows)\n- [virtualized-infinite-scrolling](../framework/react/examples/virtualized-infinite-scrolling)\n\n## Virtualization Guide\n\nThe TanStack Table packages do not come with any virtualization APIs or features built-in, but TanStack Table can easily work with other virtualization libraries like [react-window](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-window) or TanStack's own [TanStack Virtual](https://tanstack.com/virtual/v3). This guide will show some strategies for using TanStack Table with TanStack Virtual.\n"}
